{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Svelte adapter wraps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtoolsCore"},{"type":"text","value":" in a Svelte 5 component, using Svelte's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mount()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unmount()"},{"type":"text","value":" APIs to dynamically render plugins into the correct DOM containers managed by the devtools shell."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/svelte-devtools","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"component-props","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component Props"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtools"},{"type":"text","value":" component accepts the following props, defined by the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtoolsSvelteInit"},{"type":"text","value":" interface:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prop"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"plugins"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array of plugins to render inside the devtools panel."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Partial<TanStackDevtoolsConfig>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration for the devtools shell. Sets the initial state on first load; afterwards settings are persisted in local storage."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eventBusConfig"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ClientEventBusConfig"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration for the TanStack Devtools client event bus."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"plugin-type","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Plugin Type"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each plugin in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"plugins"},{"type":"text","value":" array must conform to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin"},{"type":"text","value":" type:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin = {\n  id?: string\n  component: Component<any>\n  name: string | Component<any>\n  props?: Record<string, any>\n  defaultOpen?: boolean\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" (optional)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unique identifier for the plugin."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"component"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Component<any>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Svelte component to render as the plugin panel content. It receives the shared "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"theme"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"devtoolsOpen"},{"type":"text","value":" props."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string | Component<any>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Display name for the tab title. A custom Svelte component receives the same merged plugin props."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, any>"},{"type":"text","value":" (optional)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Additional props merged with the shared plugin props when the component mounts."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultOpen"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"},{"type":"text","value":" (optional)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether this plugin tab should be open by default."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"key-difference-from-other-frameworks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key Difference from Other Frameworks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Svelte adapter uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"component"},{"type":"text","value":" (a Svelte component reference) instead of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"render"},{"type":"text","value":" (a JSX element) in plugin definitions. It passes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ theme, devtoolsOpen, ...plugin.props }"},{"type":"text","value":" to the component through Svelte's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mount()"},{"type":"text","value":" API."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the core renders a plugin again, the adapter updates the existing Svelte host with the latest component and props. If the component identity is unchanged, its state and lifecycle remain intact. The adapter unmounts the host when the plugin is destroyed or the Devtools instance shuts down."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<!-- Svelte: pass component reference + props -->\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n  import { SvelteQueryDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/svelte-query-devtools'\n\n  const plugins = [\n    {\n      name: 'Svelte Query',\n      component: SvelteQueryDevtoolsPanel,\n      props: { style: 'height: 100%' },\n    },\n  ]\n</script>\n\n<TanStackDevtools {plugins} />","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"exports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exports"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/svelte-devtools"},{"type":"text","value":" package exports:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- The main Svelte component that renders the devtools panel."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (type) -- The type for plugin definitions."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtoolsSvelteInit"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (type) -- The props interface for the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtools"},{"type":"text","value":" component."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The package depends on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/devtools"},{"type":"text","value":" (the core package), which provides "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtoolsCore"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackDevtoolsConfig"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ClientEventBusConfig"},{"type":"text","value":", and other core utilities."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"component-props","text":"Component Props","level":2},{"id":"plugin-type","text":"Plugin Type","level":2},{"id":"key-difference-from-other-frameworks","text":"Key Difference from Other Frameworks","level":2},{"id":"exports","text":"Exports","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe Svelte adapter wraps `TanStackDevtoolsCore` in a Svelte 5 component, using Svelte's `mount()` and `unmount()` APIs to dynamically render plugins into the correct DOM containers managed by the devtools shell.\n\n## Installation\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/svelte-devtools\n```\n\n## Component Props\n\nThe `TanStackDevtools` component accepts the following props, defined by the `TanStackDevtoolsSvelteInit` interface:\n\n| Prop | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `plugins` | `TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin[]` | Array of plugins to render inside the devtools panel. |\n| `config` | `Partial<TanStackDevtoolsConfig>` | Configuration for the devtools shell. Sets the initial state on first load; afterwards settings are persisted in local storage. |\n| `eventBusConfig` | `ClientEventBusConfig` | Configuration for the TanStack Devtools client event bus. |\n\n## Plugin Type\n\nEach plugin in the `plugins` array must conform to the `TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin` type:\n\n```ts\ntype TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin = {\n  id?: string\n  component: Component<any>\n  name: string | Component<any>\n  props?: Record<string, any>\n  defaultOpen?: boolean\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `id` | `string` (optional) | Unique identifier for the plugin. |\n| `component` | `Component<any>` | The Svelte component to render as the plugin panel content. It receives the shared `theme` and `devtoolsOpen` props. |\n| `name` | `string \\| Component<any>` | Display name for the tab title. A custom Svelte component receives the same merged plugin props. |\n| `props` | `Record<string, any>` (optional) | Additional props merged with the shared plugin props when the component mounts. |\n| `defaultOpen` | `boolean` (optional) | Whether this plugin tab should be open by default. |\n\n## Key Difference from Other Frameworks\n\nThe Svelte adapter uses `component` (a Svelte component reference) instead of `render` (a JSX element) in plugin definitions. It passes `{ theme, devtoolsOpen, ...plugin.props }` to the component through Svelte's `mount()` API.\n\nWhen the core renders a plugin again, the adapter updates the existing Svelte host with the latest component and props. If the component identity is unchanged, its state and lifecycle remain intact. The adapter unmounts the host when the plugin is destroyed or the Devtools instance shuts down.\n\n```svelte\n<!-- Svelte: pass component reference + props -->\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n  import { SvelteQueryDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/svelte-query-devtools'\n\n  const plugins = [\n    {\n      name: 'Svelte Query',\n      component: SvelteQueryDevtoolsPanel,\n      props: { style: 'height: 100%' },\n    },\n  ]\n</script>\n\n<TanStackDevtools {plugins} />\n```\n\n## Exports\n\nThe `@tanstack/svelte-devtools` package exports:\n\n- **`TanStackDevtools`** -- The main Svelte component that renders the devtools panel.\n- **`TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin`** (type) -- The type for plugin definitions.\n- **`TanStackDevtoolsSvelteInit`** (type) -- The props interface for the `TanStackDevtools` component.\n\nThe package depends on `@tanstack/devtools` (the core package), which provides `TanStackDevtoolsCore`, `TanStackDevtoolsConfig`, `ClientEventBusConfig`, and other core utilities.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: TanStack Devtools Svelte Adapter\nid: adapter\n---\n\nThe Svelte adapter wraps `TanStackDevtoolsCore` in a Svelte 5 component, using Svelte's `mount()` and `unmount()` APIs to dynamically render plugins into the correct DOM containers managed by the devtools shell.\n\n## Installation\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/svelte-devtools\n```\n\n## Component Props\n\nThe `TanStackDevtools` component accepts the following props, defined by the `TanStackDevtoolsSvelteInit` interface:\n\n| Prop | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `plugins` | `TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin[]` | Array of plugins to render inside the devtools panel. |\n| `config` | `Partial<TanStackDevtoolsConfig>` | Configuration for the devtools shell. Sets the initial state on first load; afterwards settings are persisted in local storage. |\n| `eventBusConfig` | `ClientEventBusConfig` | Configuration for the TanStack Devtools client event bus. |\n\n## Plugin Type\n\nEach plugin in the `plugins` array must conform to the `TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin` type:\n\n```ts\ntype TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin = {\n  id?: string\n  component: Component<any>\n  name: string | Component<any>\n  props?: Record<string, any>\n  defaultOpen?: boolean\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `id` | `string` (optional) | Unique identifier for the plugin. |\n| `component` | `Component<any>` | The Svelte component to render as the plugin panel content. It receives the shared `theme` and `devtoolsOpen` props. |\n| `name` | `string \\| Component<any>` | Display name for the tab title. A custom Svelte component receives the same merged plugin props. |\n| `props` | `Record<string, any>` (optional) | Additional props merged with the shared plugin props when the component mounts. |\n| `defaultOpen` | `boolean` (optional) | Whether this plugin tab should be open by default. |\n\n## Key Difference from Other Frameworks\n\nThe Svelte adapter uses `component` (a Svelte component reference) instead of `render` (a JSX element) in plugin definitions. It passes `{ theme, devtoolsOpen, ...plugin.props }` to the component through Svelte's `mount()` API.\n\nWhen the core renders a plugin again, the adapter updates the existing Svelte host with the latest component and props. If the component identity is unchanged, its state and lifecycle remain intact. The adapter unmounts the host when the plugin is destroyed or the Devtools instance shuts down.\n\n```svelte\n<!-- Svelte: pass component reference + props -->\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { TanStackDevtools } from '@tanstack/svelte-devtools'\n  import { SvelteQueryDevtoolsPanel } from '@tanstack/svelte-query-devtools'\n\n  const plugins = [\n    {\n      name: 'Svelte Query',\n      component: SvelteQueryDevtoolsPanel,\n      props: { style: 'height: 100%' },\n    },\n  ]\n</script>\n\n<TanStackDevtools {plugins} />\n```\n\n## Exports\n\nThe `@tanstack/svelte-devtools` package exports:\n\n- **`TanStackDevtools`** -- The main Svelte component that renders the devtools panel.\n- **`TanStackDevtoolsSveltePlugin`** (type) -- The type for plugin definitions.\n- **`TanStackDevtoolsSvelteInit`** (type) -- The props interface for the `TanStackDevtools` component.\n\nThe package depends on `@tanstack/devtools` (the core package), which provides `TanStackDevtoolsCore`, `TanStackDevtoolsConfig`, `ClientEventBusConfig`, and other core utilities.\n"}
